ted` from `candidate/test/windows-permit/helpers/ow-fixture.mjs`. They expect:\n  - the default fixture plan reaches `migration-evidence`;\n  - a service-writable config directory (and the BA/SY-only directory) is refused with `StorageUnqualified` and the message \"config directory ACL\";\n  - a service-writable release manifest or migration evidence is refused with `TrustInputUnsafe`;\n  - leaving `owned-durable-state.mjs` out of the manifest gives `ReleaseUnpinned`;\n  - an oversized existing config is refused without any unbounded read.\n\n  So the default fixture has to stay NT SERVICE, and the SYSTEM-task case needs its own fixture path.\n- **What needs changing:** only three files use the identity, ACL, config and migration code: `operator-effects-config.mjs`, `install-operator-effects.mjs` and the ow fixture/test. The two root-repaired trust paths, `chain.mjs` (79771c6c…), the r12 repairs and the bundles don't need to change.\n- **The SYSTEM trust boundary:**\n  - `aclProblem` already counts SYSTEM as a trusted writer, so a SYSTEM identity needs read-grant groups chosen for its own token.\n  - `stateAclProblem` and `createStateDirScript` would currently add a duplicate SYSTEM entry. For SYSTEM they need to expect exactly two entries: SYSTEM and Administrators with full control.\n- **Old-writer exclusion:** I can't prove continuous exclusion from source. Two things are honestly unknown from the target observation:\n  - the old process's effective NODE_DIR;\n  - whether the task actually started that process.\n\n  So against today's evidence (task enabled and running), a correct installer has to refuse.\n\nBecause the cutoff happened while I was planning the exclusion observations, I'd like to confirm scope before writing code. My proposal:\n\n1. **Identity:** an explicit process account plus launcher pair. `NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM` is accepted only with the reviewed `\\Enclave\\Node` task, and `NT SERVICE\\<name>` only with its own service. Nothing else is accepted.\n2. **Config/receipt:** bump the config to /3 so it carries the launcher identity, the retired process's PID and creation time, the exact reconciled legacy state, the release-manifest hash and the transition-evidence hash.\n3. **Installer:** require a pinned local-owner transition record, then refuse unless a fresh bounded read-only check matches it at preflight and again just before the config is written. If the old writer's NODE_DIR basis is unknown, refuse and name the missing observation.\n4. **Startup:** the agent re-checks the same bindings before its storage probe. It doesn't create, reset or switch state, and Stop and read-only reconciliation stay as they are.\n5. **Tests, report and closure:** portable tests with labelled TEST injected boundaries, then the R3 report and closure, with no run results or hashes claimed.\n\nShould I go ahead on that basis, or would you like a narrower slice, for example identity/ACL support plus an explicit refusal for cutover?","ttft_ms":3949,"type":"result","duration_ms":872196,"uuid":"29d1f6ef-78d6-44e4-922e-e45ae1516923","ttft_stream_ms":3377,"time_to_request_ms":299,"first_content_frame_ms":3378,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
